## RadBioNet LLM Configuration
## Copy this file, fill in your credentials, and save as llm_config.R
## For web deployment, set the environment variables on your server (see below).
## The app checks in this order:
##   1. Environment variables (best for production servers)
##   2. This config file (convenient for simple deployments)
##   3. Manual UI settings (click gear icon in chat)

## --- Option A: Set these environment variables on your server ---
## In terminal before launching R:
##   export RADBIO_API_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
##   export RADBIO_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here
##   export RADBIO_MODEL=deepseek-chat
##   export RADBIO_BACKEND=openai

## --- Option B: Uncomment and edit below for a simple config file ---

# LLM_BACKEND <- "openai"              # "auto", "ollama", or "openai"
# LLM_API_URL <- "https://api.deepseek.com"
# LLM_API_KEY <- "sk-your-deepseek-api-key"
# LLM_MODEL   <- "deepseek-chat"

## --- Free API Providers ---
## DeepSeek:    https://api.deepseek.com        model: deepseek-chat
## SiliconFlow: https://api.siliconflow.cn      model: deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V3
## Groq:        https://api.groq.com/openai     model: llama3-70b-8192
